# D3.js Bubble Chart with Force Simulation

## Overview
Create bubble charts using D3.js v6 with force simulation for clustering bubbles by category.

## Key Concepts

### 1. Force Simulation Setup
```javascript
const simulation = d3.forceSimulation(data)
    .force("charge", d3.forceManyBody().strength(5))
    .force("center", d3.forceCenter(width / 2, height / 2))
    .force("collision", d3.forceCollide().radius(d => radiusScale(d.value) + 2))
    .force("x", d3.forceX().x(d => xPositions[d.category]).strength(0.3))
    .force("y", d3.forceY().y(d => yPositions[d.category]).strength(0.3))
    .on("tick", ticked);
```

### 2. Clustering by Category with forceX/forceY
```javascript
// Create cluster centers for each category
const categories = [...new Set(data.map(d => d.sector))];
const clusterCenters = {};
categories.forEach((cat, i) => {
    const angle = (2 * Math.PI * i) / categories.length;
    clusterCenters[cat] = {
        x: width/2 + Math.cos(angle) * 150,
        y: height/2 + Math.sin(angle) * 150
    };
});

// Apply forces toward cluster centers
simulation
    .force("x", d3.forceX(d => clusterCenters[d.sector].x).strength(0.2))
    .force("y", d3.forceY(d => clusterCenters[d.sector].y).strength(0.2));
```

### 3. Radius Scale for Bubble Size
```javascript
const radiusScale = d3.scaleSqrt()
    .domain([0, d3.max(data, d => d.marketCap)])
    .range([5, 50]);
```

### 4. Color Scale for Categories
```javascript
const colorScale = d3.scaleOrdinal()
    .domain(categories)
    .range(d3.schemeCategory10);
```

### 5. Creating Bubbles
```javascript
const bubbles = svg.selectAll("circle")
    .data(data)
    .enter()
    .append("circle")
    .attr("r", d => radiusScale(d.marketCap))
    .attr("fill", d => colorScale(d.sector))
    .attr("stroke", "#333")
    .attr("stroke-width", 1);
```

### 6. Tick Function for Animation
```javascript
function ticked() {
    bubbles
        .attr("cx", d => d.x)
        .attr("cy", d => d.y);
    labels
        .attr("x", d => d.x)
        .attr("y", d => d.y);
}
```

### 7. forceCollide to Prevent Overlap
```javascript
simulation.force("collision", d3.forceCollide()
    .radius(d => radiusScale(d.marketCap) + 2)
    .strength(1));
```

### 8. Adding Labels Inside Bubbles
```javascript
const labels = svg.selectAll("text.label")
    .data(data)
    .enter()
    .append("text")
    .attr("class", "label")
    .attr("text-anchor", "middle")
    .attr("dy", ".35em")
    .style("font-size", d => Math.min(radiusScale(d.marketCap) / 2, 12) + "px")
    .text(d => d.ticker);
```

## Best Practices
- Use `d3.scaleSqrt()` for bubble radius to ensure area is proportional to value
- Set appropriate force strengths (0.1-0.5) for smooth clustering
- Use `forceCollide` with slightly larger radius to prevent overlap
- Keep cluster centers reasonably close to chart center
